my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello world
hxllo world
hlllo world
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{/ with regex metacharacters matches patterns},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/search_regex`

**/pattern** supports regex metacharacters. `h.llo` uses `.` to match any single character, matching "hello", "hxllo", and "hlllo".

**Keys:** `/h.llo\n`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0
- Three lines with similar but different text

**after_regex_search.png**
- Cursor on first match "hello" on line 1, col 0
- All three lines highlighted: "hello", "hxllo", "hlllo" (each matches `h.llo`)
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('/h.llo\n');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_regex_search');
    },
}
